ir  story is but then it gets even more  strange when we find out that an agent  of sword  is watching them like a tv show on a  television  now if you're not familiar with what  sword is it is the space  counterpart to shield sword stands for  sentient  world observation and response  department and they seem to be  monitoring wanda and vision  now things start to really pick up in  episode 2 where there are references and  easter eggs to three  villains the first one is actually  spotted in the intro of episode 2  right after the funny bed scene opening  if you pause the show  during the intro at 3 27 when vision  is phasing through the floor you can see  that under the floor  is a helmet of some sort now originally  a lot of us thought that this was  galactus helmet however this looks a lot  more like  the grim reaper's helmet this is villain  number one  and what's really interesting about this  is that grim reaper in the comics  is the brother of wonder man and  basically what happens in the comics is  that vision's brainwaves came from  wonder man so grim reaper views vision  as an abomination that stole a part of  his brother  now another really interesting thing  about grim reaper is that at one point  in time he has worked for hydra  and ultron and i'll go over that in just  a bit when we talk about the hydra scene  in episode 2.  as we get into this episode we see that  wanda and vision are doing a talent show  that is for the children and this is an  ongoing theme  from here wanda goes off to the planning  committee meeting for the talent show  and vision goes off to a neighborhood  watch meeting but before wanda goes out  we see that she finds a helicopter  a helicopter that is in color red and  yellow and it has  the sword logo on it now it was revealed  in the first episode that sword is  indeed  monitoring her and we have seen from the  trailers that there's a helicopter that  looks exactly like this that kind of  gets sucked into  this magical bubble that is surrounding  west view so this is that helicopter and  eventually we will see the scene where  it gets sucked into this reality  but wanda is starting to realize that  things aren't quite what they seem  and things are getting a little weird  but here is where we get  possibly the biggest easter egg and  reveal and hint  towards who the villain of the show  actually is  during the planning meeting the  character dottie says  the devil is in the details bev and then  agnes  again who we believe to be agatha  harkness  leans over to wanda and says that's not  the only place he is  now for those of you who have been  watching my videos leading up to one  division  you know what i'm about to say this is a  reference to  mephisto mephisto is the devil  of the marvel universe he is the ruler  of the hell realm  and he has a huge tie-in to wanda  specifically when it comes to her  children and children  are being stressed in this episode and  the house of m  story remember marvel does everything  super  intentionally and you're not just going  to drop the devil's name  and then a one-liner like that from  agatha immediately after without it  meaning something now this episode goes  on to stress  for the children it stresses children  and then at the end of this episode  wanda is suddenly pregnant now how  exactly is this possible since  vision is a synthesiod well in the  comics wanda is actually pregnant with  the shards of mephisto's soul and  eventually  after wanda has her kids mephisto wants  those shards  back and he ultimately would take them  back  wanda loses her kids this leads her to  eventually  go insane and it leads us up to the  house of m  storyline where she utters the famous  words no more mutants  from there she creates her own reality  where her family  is the rulers and i believe that that is  what we are working up to here  in fact we did get a little bit of a  house of m  vibe specifically at the end of this  episode when wanda and vision find out  that they're pregnant they hear a noise  outside  this is where things start to get that  horror aspect again and get very creepy  they go outside and in the street the  beekeeper comes out of the sewer  wanda gets scared and sees how this  could jeopardize her perfect  reality and she says no and then  she alters reality she changes reality  to where that person  never existed he didn't come into the  picture after they found out that  they're pregnant  now this pretty much mirrors the comics  where wanda says  no more mutants and then changes reality  in the show  she says no and then changes reality  so we know that a house of m story is  kind of taking place  within this episode and future episodes  now marvel doesn't exactly  copy the entire story from the comics  they take pieces of the story and make  their own  so it's not going to be exactly the same  but one thing is for certain  and that is that mephisto wants wanda to  have kids  however why that is is unclear at this  point but let's not forget that in the  loki trailer we did see a mephisto  easter egg in one scene in the trailer  we can see a stained glass  devil there's no real reason for marvel  to put this  in a show or a scene without it meaning  something and mephisto is too big of a  villain to just have for one  show which is why i say not only is he  going to be the big villain of this  series along with grim reaper and hydra  but he's going to be the villain of the  entire phase 4 and  possibly phase 5 appearing in other  shows and then a movie  now going back to hydra we do have this  hydra scene in this episode which is a  callback to how wanda got her powers  the easter egg 4 hydra comes in the form  of a commercial  that is a strucker hydra watch now  strucker if you recall  in avengers age of ultron is baron von  strucker  the hydra scientist who experimented on  wanda and quicksilver  and is responsible for giving them their  powers through the mind stone of course  but this most likely isn't a simple  callback hydra most likely has something  to do with the wandevision series and i  believe  that this beekeeper that came out of the  ground could be a hydra  agent somehow wanda is locked inside of  this bubble reality we've seen from the  trailers that there is clearly some type  of force field that is created by energy  protecting the city and the fact that  this person comes from  under the ground through a sewer could  mean that this was the only way that he  could  actually get through this energy field  was to go under it  now why exactly is this person a bee  keeper that's unclear right now  it could be that he is actually a  villain from the spider-man comics  the villain swarm now swarm's real name  is fritz  von mayer and he's a german scientist  who worked for adolf  hitler so they could change his story  just a little bit in the marvel  cinematic universe to make it to where  he's a hydra scientist  and this could be him that we see in  this episode but  at the same time it could very well be a  sword agent who is trying to break into  this reality  and see what's going on and try to help  wanda and i always say try and help  wanda and not want to envision because i  truly believe  that vision is not alive it's too early  to tell but i don't think he's back from  the dead  he could possibly be an illusion or he  could be the product of  mephisto we'll have to wait for more  episodes until we find out what exactly  is going on but those are the three  villains that i think were revealed in  the first  two episodes of wanda vision let me know  what you thought about the first two  episodes of wandavision in the comments  down below and let me know what you  think about these three villains  being in one division more breakdowns of  the first two episodes coming later on  this week so don't forget to subscribe  so you don't miss out on any of the  videos  don't forget to like the video and for  live updates you can follow me on  in